    new "精疲力竭，却依然紧紧相拥，这对恋人瘫倒在冰冷的石地板上。"

    old "The cold press of stone against flesh was a welcome feeling."
    new "冰冷的石头紧贴着肌肤，这种感觉令人感到慰藉。"

    old "Each loudly breathed, both trying to regain their composure."
    new "两人都在大口喘气，试图平复心绪。"

    old "It would take some time more before the first dared to break the silence."
    new "要过一段时间，才会有人敢打破这份沉默。"

    old "This...I don't know what I was thinking."
    new "这……我不知道我当时在想什么。"

    old "You weren't thinking. For once, maybe you just did something because you wanted to."
    new "你根本没在思考。也许这一次，你只是单纯地因为想要而做了某事。"

    old "You stay trapped long enough, even in a place like this, you're bound to try and break free. It's only natural."
    new "被困得够久，哪怕是在这种地方，你也难免会想要挣脱。这再自然不过了。"

    old "This is something you do often, out there in the real world?"
    new "你在外面的现实世界里也经常这样吗？"

    old "No, I wouldn't say often."
    new "不，我不会说经常。"

    old "Sarah felt Samayra's fingers intertwining with hers."
    new "莎拉感觉到萨玛拉的手指与她的交缠在一起。"

    old "She tried to remember. Had she reached out, or had Samayra? She no longer knew."
    new "她试图回忆。是她主动伸出手，还是萨玛拉？她已经记不清了。"

    old "Their fingers interlaced, each laid on their back, staring up towards the ceiling."
    new "十指紧扣，两人各自仰卧，凝视着天花板。"

    old "Their heavy breathing slowly subsided."
    new "他们沉重的呼吸渐渐平息下来。"

    old "In the cold air. The comfortable silence. Sarah found a peace coming over her."
    new "在冰冷的空气中，在那舒适的寂静里，莎拉感到一种宁静悄然降临。"

    old "It felt to her like a weight, sitting atop her chest for so long she had nearly forgotten it was there, suddenly lifted."
    new "那感觉就像一直压在她心口的一块巨石，久到她几乎忘了它的存在，此刻却突然被移开了。"

    old "Had she been like this, she wondered, all these last years? Had that loneliness in Xan's home left wounds she had grown to forget?"
    new "她不禁想，过去这些年里，自己难道一直是这样吗？在赞的家中，那份孤独是否留下了伤口，以至于她早已将其遗忘？"

    old "She could feel a part of herself returning or reviving. The person she had been before."
    new "她能感觉到自己的一部分正在回归，或者说复苏。那是她从前那个人的模样。"

    old "A tear ran down her cheek, unseen and unnoticed."
    new "一滴泪顺着她的脸颊滑落，无人看见，也无人察觉。"

    old "In the dark, she remembered parts of the person she had killed to become the person she now was."
    new "在黑暗中，她记起了为了成为如今的自己而扼杀掉的、属于旧日自我的那些部分。"

    old "I think we should go back to my room. I'll need to be rested for tomorrow."
    new "我想我们该回我房间了。明天我需要休息好。"

    old "Sarah watched as Samayra wordlessly stood up and began to dress herself. Sarah followed after."
    new "莎拉看着萨玛拉无声地站起身来，开始整理衣物。莎拉跟在后面。"

    old "Samayra turned to lead her back, but before she could, Sarah seized the princess by her wrist."
    new "萨玛拉转身准备带路回去，但还没等她行动，莎拉便一把抓住了公主的手腕。"

    old "She pulled Samayra close and kissed her."
    new "她拉近萨玛拉，吻了她。"

    old "Don't think it didn't mean anything to me. Because it did."
    new "别以为这对我毫无意义。因为确实有意义。"

    old "Even in the dark, Sarah could make out Samayra's smile."
    new "即使在黑暗中，莎拉也能看清萨玛拉的笑容。"

    old "Together, the two made their way back to Sarah's room."
    new "两人一同回到了莎拉的房间。"

    old "Unbeknownst to Samayra, Sarah traced her finger across the walls as she walked, leaving a soft trace of lingering magic, leading from the vault back to her room."
    new "萨玛拉并不知道，莎拉在行走时用手指沿着墙壁划过，留下了一缕柔和而持久的魔法痕迹，从密室一直延伸回她的房间。"

    old "Sarah returned to her room and watched Samayra dissapear back into the secret tunnels, too nervous to speak much of what had transpired between them."
    new "莎拉回到房间，看着萨玛拉消失在秘密隧道中，因太过紧张而未能多言他们之间发生的事。"

    old "As she watched the walls close and the passage vanish, Sarah began inspecting her room again."
    new "看着墙壁合拢、通道消失，莎拉又开始仔细打量起她的房间。"

    old "It suddenly looked very lonely."
    new "它突然显得非常孤寂。"

    old "She returned to her bed and tried to force herself to sleep."
    new "她回到床上，试图强迫自己入睡。"

    old "Only after many hours did she finally succeed."
    new "直到过了好几个小时，她才终于成功入睡。"

    old "Push Samayra"
    new "推萨梅拉"

    old "Sarah softly pushed Samayra."
    new "莎拉轻轻推了萨玛拉一把。"

    old "The princess, caught by surprise, stumbled back."
    new "公主猝不及防，踉跄后退。"

    old "Don't act like you know me."
    new "别装得好像你很了解我似的。"

    old "We've seen each other around the palace a few times, spoken even less."
    new "我们在宫里见过几次面，但交谈却少得可怜。"

    old "I've lost more than you've ever cherised."
    new "我失去的，比你珍视的任何东西都要多。"

    old "You're just a spoiled princess, playing a poor game of politics."
    new "你不过是个被宠坏的公主，把政治当成一场过家家的游戏。"

    old "Sarah could see an anger growing in Samayra's eyes."
    new "莎拉看到萨玛拉眼中怒火渐起。"

    old "So you won't keep your word?"
    new "所以你不会信守诺言了？"

    old "Sarah waited for a moment before answering."
    new "莎拉停顿片刻，才开口回答。"

    old "She knew she could go to Xan, tell him that she had discovered the location of the vault, and he would almost certainly abandon Bagrad."
    new "她知道她可以去找桑，告诉她自己发现了金库的位置，而桑几乎肯定会抛弃巴格拉德。"

    old "Still, Sarah felt pity for Samayra. The girl was scared, and right to be so."
    new "尽管如此，莎拉还是对萨玛拉心生怜悯。这女孩很害怕，而且她的恐惧并非毫无来由。"

    old "Sarah had walked away from her own country when they needed her most. She had vowed never to do so again."
    new "莎拉曾在国家最需要她的时候选择离开。她曾发誓绝不再犯同样的错误。"

    old "She would be loyal to that vow."
    new "她会忠于那个誓言。"

    old "I'll keep my word, and I will protect you and your family."
    new "我会信守诺言，保护你和你的家人。"

    old "But I won't do so because you bribed me, or we struck some kind of deal. I'll do it because it's the right thing to do."
    new "但我这么做不是因为你贿赂了我，也不是因为我们达成了什么交易。我这么做是因为这是正确的事。"

    old "These words seemed to calm Samayra down."
    new "这些话似乎让萨玛拉平静了下来。"

    old "Good, that's all I ever wanted."
    new "很好，这正是我所求的。"

    old "Sarah looked around the dark tunnels. She wondered how many layers of stone were build on top of them. A frightening thought."
    new "莎拉环顾四周，看着这些黑暗的隧道。她不禁在想，上面究竟堆叠了多少层石头。这是一个令人恐惧的念头。"

    old "I've seen enough of this place. Take me back to my room."
    new "我看够了这地方。带我回房间。"

    old "Dutifully, and without saying much more, Samayra took Sarah back to her room."
    new "萨玛拉顺从地照办，没有再多说什么，便把莎拉送回了她的房间。"

    old "It suddenly looked so very lonely."
    new "它突然显得如此孤寂。"

    old "Perhaps she had been too harsh on the girl."
    new "也许她对那个女孩太严厉了。"

    old "Sarah had no desire to get lost in any secret tunnels, certainly not the day before a battle."
    new "莎拉可没有兴趣去探索什么秘密隧道，尤其是在大战的前一天。"

    old "It's impressive, but I'd rather stay here for now. I'll need to be well rested for tomorrow."
    new "确实令人印象深刻，但我还是想留在这里。明天我需要养精蓄锐。"

    old "Ooh...I understand."
    new "哦……我明白了。"

    old "Samayra seemed dissapointed at Sarah's reply."
    new "萨玛拉对莎拉的答复显得有些失望。"

    old "Sarah struggled not to feel bad for the girl. So much of her seemed to remind her of herself."
    new "莎拉努力克制住对女孩的同情。她身上的许多特质都让莎拉想起了曾经的自己。"

    old "Well, I mean, you don't have to go right away."
    new "我的意思是，你不必马上就走。"

    old "Sure, I can stay for a bit."
    new "当然，我可以待一会儿。"

    old "I thought we could just talk. I feel like I should know you better."
    new "我以为我们可以只是聊聊天。我觉得我应该更了解你一些。"

    old "Ooh, why is that?"
    new "哦，为什么这么说？"

    old "I keep thinking about our moment in the garden."
    new "我总想起我们在花园里的那段时光。"

    old "She could see Samayra smile as she looked away."
    new "她移开视线时，萨玛拉露出了微笑。"

    old "Ooh, that..."
    new "哦，那个……"

    old "Have you been thinking about it?"
    new "你有在想那件事吗？"

    old "Samayra kept her eyes fixed to the floor."
    new "萨玛拉一直盯着地板。"

    old "She suddenly looked up at Sarah. Her eyes were watery."
    new "她突然抬起头看向莎拉。她的眼眶湿润。"

    old "Why did you do it?"
    new "你为什么要这么做？"

    old "It felt right, in the moment. I don't think there was more to it."
    new "当时觉得那样做是对的。我不认为其中还有什么别的原因。"

    old "Was it because you liked my dancing?"
    new "是因为你喜欢我的舞蹈吗？"

    old "Maybe, that too, but it also reminded me of home. Of a place I hadn't thought about in a long time."
    new "也许吧，这也算一个原因，但它也让我想起了家。想起了一个我许久未曾想起的地方。"

    old "You made me go back there in a way, and it just made me feel very happy."
    new "你在某种程度上让我回到了那里，这让我感到非常快乐。"

    old "I hadn't felt that happy in a long time, and then...I guess I just lost track of myself."
    new "我已经很久没有感到这么开心了，然后……我想我只是有些忘乎所以。"

    old "If it upset you, I'll apologize."
    new "如果这让你感到不快，我会道歉。"

    old "The princess was quiet for a moment."
    new "公主沉默了片刻。"

    old "No, it didn't upset me. Surprise me, maybe."
    new "不，我没生气。只是有点意外罢了。"

    old "I never kissed anyone before, so..."
    new "我以前从没吻过任何人，所以……"

    old "Sarah let her eyes slide across Samayra's body."
    new "莎拉的目光滑过萨玛拉的身体。"

    old "She was so beautiful, it was hard to imagine she could be so inexperienced, and yet, she had also been kept isolated from the world. Perhaps Sarah should have known."
    new "她美得令人难以置信，让人很难想象她会如此缺乏经验，然而，她也一直与世隔绝。也许莎拉本该知道的。"

    old "How do you feel about it?"
    new "你对这件事感觉如何？"

    old "Samayra smiled at Sarah."
    new "萨玛拉对莎拉笑了笑。"

    old "You just said I made you feel happy, like you haven't been happy in a long time."
    new "你刚才说，我让你感到快乐，就像你已经很久没有感受过快乐一样。"

    old "I guess, I think that's how you made me feel."
    new "我想，这就是你让我感觉到的。"

    old "The two were silent for a while, each processing what now grew between them."
    new "两人沉默了一会儿，各自消化着彼此间逐渐滋长的情愫。"

    old "Samayra was hesitant for a moment, but gave in and walked up to the bed."
    new "萨玛拉犹豫了片刻，但最终妥协，走向床边。"

    old "You always look so lonely walking around here."
    new "你在这里走来走去的时候，看起来总是那么孤单。"

    old "Sarah could see Samayra wrestling in her mind. Did she dare?"
    new "莎拉看得出，萨玛拉内心正在激烈挣扎。她敢吗？"

    old "I'm not sure..."
    new "我不太确定……"

    old "But Sarah was persistent. She began to pull on Samayra's hands, dragging her partly into the bed."
    new "但莎拉很执着。她开始拉扯萨玛拉的手，将她半拖进床里。"

    old "Depending on how tomorrow goes this might be our last night on this earth."
    new "如果明天一切顺利，这可能是我们在这个世界上度过的最后一夜。"

    old "We might not get another chance."
    new "我们可能不会再有第二次机会了。"

    old "Once in the bed, the two crawled up to each other. Sarah reached out, the tips of her fingers sliding across Samayra's body."
    new "一进到床上，两人便向彼此爬近。莎拉伸出手，指尖轻轻滑过萨玛拉的身体。"

    old "Soon, Sarah and Samayra both found themselves naked under the covers of the bed."
    new "很快，莎拉和萨玛拉都发现自己赤裸地躺在被子里。"

    old "I think we'd have a lot in common."
    new "我觉得我们会有很多共同点。"

    old "Samayra eyed Sarah, inquisitively."
    new "萨玛拉好奇地打量着莎拉。"

    old "What would we have in common?"
    new "我们会有什么共同点？"

    old "More than you might think, actually."
    new "比你想象的要多得多。"

    old "Sarah smirked at Samayra, who seemed none too entertained by her cryptic answers."
    new "莎拉对萨玛拉露出意味深长的微笑，后者显然对她这些故弄玄虚的回答毫无兴趣。"

    old "If you're just going to play games, I think I will leave."
    new "如果你只是想玩这种游戏，我想我还是离开吧。"

    old "No, really, please I want you to stay."
    new "不，我是认真的，求你留下吧。"

    old "There isn't anyone to talk to here, other than Xan, and he makes for a poor audience."
    new "除了山之外，这里没人可聊，而他可不是个合格的听众。"

    old "Well, what do you want to talk about then?"
    new "好吧，那你想聊点什么？"

    old "I just want to get to know you."
    new "我只是想多了解你。"

    old "Well, ask away..."
    new "好吧，尽管问吧……"

    old "Sarah considered her question."
    new "莎拉斟酌着这个问题。"

    old "What was it like, growing up here in the palace?"
    new "在这里的宫殿里长大是什么感觉？"

    old "I don't feel like I should complain. I've never wanted for anything. Whatever thing I wanted, I would get."
    new "我觉得没什么好抱怨的。我从未缺过什么，想要任何东西都能得到。"

    old "Teachers from across the world came and taught me about all sorts of things."
    new "世界各地的老师都来教过我各种各样的东西。"

    old "They'd bring me books and trinkets from every corner of the world."
    new "他们会从世界的各个角落给我带来书籍和小玩意儿。"

    old "For a while, living here with my father and my mother was enough for me."
    new "有一段时间，和父亲母亲一起生活在这里对我来说就已经足够了。"

    old "I think I could have gone on living like that forever, honestly..."
    new "说实话，我觉得自己那样过一辈子也没什么不好……"

    old "But?"
    new "但是？"

    old "When my mother died a few years ago, I think it changed something. For me, as well as my father."
    new "几年前我母亲去世后，我觉得有些东西改变了。对我来说，还有我父亲也是。"

    old "He grew cold and distant, in a way he never had been before."
    new "他变得冷漠而疏远，这是一种前所未有的状态。"

    old "Losing my mother, but then also sort of losing my father...I was left alone in this place."
    new "失去了母亲，接着又仿佛失去了父亲……我在这地方孤身一人。"

    old "Sarah could see the sadness come over Samayra."
    new "莎拉能看到悲伤笼罩了萨玛拉。"

    old "I'm so sorry. I didn't know about your mother..."
    new "真抱歉，我不知道你母亲的事……"

    old "It's alright. It's been a few years, I've buried my grief for the most part...but father, he never seemed to move past it."
    new "没事的。已经过去几年了，我大部分时间都已经埋葬了自己的悲伤……但父亲，他似乎始终无法走出那段阴影。"

    old "It was like a wound that just...never healed."
    new "那就像一道从未愈合的伤口。"

    old "Sarah desperately wanted to connect with her."
    new "莎拉迫切地想要与她建立联系。"

    old "I can understand that."
    new "我能理解。"

    old "How? How could you understand?"
    new "怎么理解？你怎么可能理解？"

    old "Sarah hesitated, but then decided to be truthful."
    new "莎拉犹豫了一下，但最终还是决定坦诚相待。"

    old "My...my mother also died when I was young..."
    new "我……我的母亲在我年幼时也去世了……"

    old "No, it's alright. Like you, I gave it a place. But my father also struggled with it for a very long time."
    new "不，没事的。就像你一样，我也给它留了个位置。但我父亲也为此挣扎了很久。"

    old "Were you lonely?"
    new "你感到孤独吗？"

    old "I think I would have been, if it hadn't been for my brother, Thomas."
    new "我想我本来会孤独的，如果不是有我的哥哥托马斯的话。"

    old "He and I could support one another, share that pain...I think that helped each of us deal with it, heal in a better way maybe."
    new "我和他能够互相扶持，分担那份痛苦……我想这帮助了我们各自应对这一切，也许让我们以更好的方式愈合。"

    old "Samayra looked off to the far side of the room, avoiding any eye contact."
    new "萨玛拉将目光投向房间的另一侧，避免与任何人进行眼神交流。"

    old "I never had that. Maybe that would have made a difference."
    new "我从未拥有过那样的羁绊。也许那会改变一切。"

    old "What was she like?"
    new "她是个什么样的人？"

    old "Your mother. What kind of person was she?"
    new "你母亲。她是个什么样的人？"

    old "Sarah could see Samayra lighten up, a broad smile passing over her face."
    new "莎拉看到萨玛拉的神情明朗起来，脸上浮现出灿烂的笑容。"

    old "She began to tell Sarah all about her mother, and Sarah found herself transported by her words."
    new "她开始向莎拉讲述关于她母亲的一切，而莎拉则被她的话语深深吸引。"

    old "It wasn't long before Sarah found herself crying for a woman she had never met."
    new "没过多久，莎拉便为一个从未谋面的女人流下了眼泪。"

    old "By the end, Sarah had gained a new understanding of Samayra."
    new "到了最后，莎拉对萨玛拉有了全新的理解。"

    old "She wandered a massive palace, all by herself, for years on end. The loneliness both a fact of her life, as well as a punishment she inflicted on herself."
    new "她独自在巨大的宫殿里徘徊，年复一年。这种孤独既是她生活的常态，也是她施加于自身的惩罚。"

    old "Thank you for listening to me."
    new "谢谢你听我说。"

    old "It's not often that I get to talk about my mother."
    new "我很少有机会谈论我的母亲。"

    old "Sarah smiled, she was happy to see Samayra smiling as well."
    new "莎拉笑了，看到萨玛拉也在微笑，她感到很高兴。"

    old "Thank you for telling me about her."
    new "谢谢你告诉我这些。"

    old "What about your mother? What was she like?"
    new "你母亲呢？她是个什么样的人？"

    old "Sarah imagined the question would come, but had hoped to avoid it. She might still avoid it."
    new "莎拉想象着这个问题迟早会来，但她仍希望能避开它。她或许还能躲过这一劫。"

    old "It's late, Samayra. I need to get some sleep for tomorrow."
    new "太晚了，萨玛拉。我得去睡会儿，明天还有事。"

    old "I promise you, if we survive all of this, I'll talk to you about her."
    new "我向你保证，如果我们能挺过这一切，我会跟你谈谈她。"

    old "I'll keep you to that promise."
    new "我会记住你的承诺。"

    old "Sarah watched as the princess vanished into the passage that she first emerged from, and the walls closed behind her."
    new "莎拉注视着公主消失在当初她现身的那条通道里，墙壁在她身后合拢。"

